  "ai_language_tip": "Spoken Maghrebi Arabic (Darija) is the daily language, and French is widely used for business, clinics and hotels; a polite mix of French and simple Arabic works best. Amazigh (Berber) languages are spoken in parts of all three countries. English is limited outside tourism.",
  "english_ok": "rarely — Tourist hotels, riads and some younger staff in Marrakech, Casablanca, Tunis; most businesses prefer French or Darija.",
  "politeness": "Greet first ('Salam alaykum' or 'Bonjour') and ask how they are; formal 'vous' in French; 'Si/Lalla' (ma) or 'Monsieur/Madame' as titles; close with thanks ('Merci, bonne journée' / 'شكرا').",
  "name_tip": "Bookings under family name or first name; Latin spellings follow French conventions (Mohamed, Ouahid, Benali), so spell letter by letter in French.",
  "phone_tip": "ma 06/07 XX XX XX XX (+212, e.g. 06 12345678); dz 05/06/07 XX XX XX XX (+213); tn 8 digits XX XXX XXX (+216, e.g. 12345678); WhatsApp is the norm for confirmations.",
  "time_tip": "Time often given in French 24h ('19h30') or Darija ('السبعة ونص'); Morocco shifts clocks for Ramadan; confirm the clock time and day carefully during Ramadan when hours change.",
  "number_tip": "Prices and phone numbers often said in French; phone numbers read in pairs; Moroccans may quote prices in old units (rial/franc) instead of dirhams/dinars — confirm the currency amount.",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid Friday midday prayer, lunch 12:30–14:30, calls after 21:00, the hour before iftar in Ramadan, and Eid holidays; Algeria's weekend is Friday–Saturday.",
  "closed_days": "Weekend is Saturday–Sunday in ma and tn, Friday–Saturday in dz; many shops still close Friday afternoon; Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha close most businesses; summer (July–August) has reduced hours in offices (tn, dz).",
  "booking_channels": "DabaDoc for doctors (ma, dz, tn); phone and WhatsApp for restaurants, salons, garages and riads; Glovo (ma, tn), Yassir (dz) and Jumia Food-type apps for delivery; Careem/inDrive/Yassir and petit taxis for rides.",
  "voice_menu": "Telecoms (Maroc Telecom, Orange, inwi, Djezzy, Mobilis, Ooredoo, Tunisie Telecom), banks and utilities use IVR; small businesses answer directly.",
  "callback_habits": "Clinics and DabaDoc send SMS reminders; restaurants and riads confirm by WhatsApp or a call on the day.",
